# Where a checkout's own run puts every generated file (DATA_DIR's default), plus
# the pre-move layout that kept them under the library root.
data
**/.bowerbird
coverage
# Rust build artefacts, 787MB of them. The image builds the crate itself, and the
# runtime stage copies the source in for the entrypoint's tuned rebuild, so shipping
# a host-built target dir would be dead weight - and a host-built `librawshim.so`
# sitting at the path the loader checks first would shadow the image's own.
native/rawshim/target
# A local photo library and the RAW test fixtures: hundreds of MB the image has no
# use for, and the integration tests do not run in it.
.photos
test/fixtures
